# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.iml
.idea
!.idea/codeStyles

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Annotation processor output written OUTSIDE target/ by IntelliJ IDEA's own (non-Maven) build.
#
# The JPA static metamodel generator (Hibernate's, or EclipseLink's) runs as an annotation processor. Maven writes its
# output under target/generated-sources/annotations and target/generated-test-sources/test-annotations, which target/
# above already ignores. IntelliJ IDEA, when it compiles by itself rather than delegating to Maven, resolves the
# imported relative output paths (../generated-sources/annotations, ../generated-test-sources/test-annotations) against
# the wrong base, and leaves these directories at the root of a module instead. They hold nothing but regenerated code
# (the metamodel classes, Hibernate's entity/index) and are safe to delete.
#
# To stop them being created at all: Settings | Build, Execution, Deployment | Build Tools | Maven | Runner |
# "Delegate IDE build/run actions to Maven".
/generated-sources/
/generated-test-sources/
/*/generated-sources/
/*/generated-test-sources/
